# Liability cap — Acme Cloud Systems / Northwind Logistics (ACME-NW-MSA-2026)

> Module Liability_cap_acme_northwind
> Using Legal_types as T

Sources: SYN-001 (Master Services Agreement, 2026-01-01), SYN-003 (Order Form No. 1,
2026-07-01). SYN-004 (Amendment No. 1) also defines this cap and is **not** encoded here:
see `liability_cap_acme_northwind_with_amendment.catala_en` for the conflict it creates.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope LiabilityCap:
  input fees_paid_last_12mo content money
  input annual_fees content money
  input claim_type content T.ClaimType
  input claim_date content date

  internal excluded_claim condition
  internal uncapped_claim condition
  internal order_form_applies condition

  output cap content money
  output uncapped content boolean
```

## SYN-001 § 9.3 — definition of Excluded Claims

  "Excluded Claims" means claims arising from (a) breach of Section 11 (Confidentiality)
  and (b) a party's indemnity obligations for third-party intellectual property
  infringement under Section 10.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  rule excluded_claim under condition
    claim_type = T.ClaimType.Confidentiality
    or claim_type = T.ClaimType.IpIndemnity
  consequence fulfilled
```

## SYN-001 § 9.4 — matters outside every cap

  The limitations in Sections 9.2 and 9.3 do not apply to (a) a party's gross negligence
  or willful misconduct, (b) Customer's obligation to pay Fees, or (c) either party's
  liability for death or personal injury caused by its negligence. Liability for those
  matters is unlimited.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  rule uncapped_claim under condition
    claim_type = T.ClaimType.GrossNegligence
    or claim_type = T.ClaimType.UnpaidFees
    or claim_type = T.ClaimType.BodilyInjury
  consequence fulfilled
```

## SYN-003 — the Order Form governs claims from its effective date

  Order Form effective date: July 1, 2026. […] Notwithstanding Section 9.2 of the MSA,
  each party's aggregate liability arising out of or related to the Services ordered under
  this Order Form shall not exceed three hundred percent (300%) of the Annual Fees stated
  above.

The Order Form controls by authority of SYN-001 § 14.3 (Order of Precedence), which is why
the definitions below are declared as exceptions rather than as competing definitions.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  rule order_form_applies under condition
    claim_date >= |2026-07-01|
  consequence fulfilled
```

## SYN-001 § 9.2 — the base cap

  Except as provided in Sections 9.3 and 9.4, each party's aggregate liability arising out
  of or related to this Agreement shall not exceed the total Fees paid or payable by
  Customer in the twelve (12) months preceding the first event giving rise to the claim.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  label msa_9_2
  definition cap equals fees_paid_last_12mo
```

## SYN-001 § 9.2 and § 9.4 — liability is capped unless § 9.4 applies

  Except as provided in Sections 9.3 and 9.4 […] The limitations in Sections 9.2 and 9.3
  do not apply to (a) a party's gross negligence or willful misconduct, (b) Customer's
  obligation to pay Fees, or (c) either party's liability for death or personal injury
  caused by its negligence.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  definition uncapped equals false
```

## SYN-001 § 9.3 — the Excluded Claims cap, before the Order Form

  For Excluded Claims, each party's aggregate liability shall not exceed two hundred
  percent (200%) of the total Fees paid or payable by Customer in the twelve (12) months
  preceding the first event giving rise to the claim.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  label msa_9_3 exception msa_9_2
  definition cap
    under condition excluded_claim and not order_form_applies
    consequence equals fees_paid_last_12mo * 2.0
```

## SYN-003 § 5.1 — the Order Form's general cap

  Notwithstanding Section 9.2 of the MSA, each party's aggregate liability arising out of
  or related to the Services ordered under this Order Form shall not exceed three hundred
  percent (300%) of the Annual Fees stated above.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  label of_5_1 exception msa_9_2
  definition cap
    under condition
      order_form_applies and not excluded_claim and not uncapped_claim
    consequence equals annual_fees * 3.0
```

## SYN-003 § 5.2 — the Order Form's supercap for Excluded Claims

  Notwithstanding Section 9.3 of the MSA, each party's aggregate liability for Excluded
  Claims shall not exceed five hundred percent (500%) of the Annual Fees stated above.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  label of_5_2 exception msa_9_2
  definition cap
    under condition order_form_applies and excluded_claim
    consequence equals annual_fees * 5.0
```

## SYN-001 § 9.4 and SYN-003 § 5.3 — unlimited liability

  Section 9.4 of the MSA (unlimited liability for gross negligence, willful misconduct,
  payment obligations, and death or personal injury) is unchanged.

`cap` still has to be defined for the interpreter, so it is set to the fees figure and
`uncapped` is the output that governs: a caller that ignores `uncapped` and reads `cap`
alone is reading the wrong number, which is why both are outputs.

```catala
scope LiabilityCap:
  label carve_out exception msa_9_2
  definition cap
    under condition uncapped_claim
    consequence equals fees_paid_last_12mo

  exception
  definition uncapped
    under condition uncapped_claim
    consequence equals true
```
